TacticPod command menu (115200 baud; finish each command with Enter):
  IMU ON       - print IMU readings at 10 Hz
  IMU OFF      - stop printing; sampling continues (100 Hz when recording)
  RECORD START / RECORD STOP / RECORD STATUS - append binary IMU at 100 Hz
  RECORD READ  - export committed recordings as CSV while stopped
  RECORD ERASE - warn before explicitly confirmed recording-area erase
  DIAG         - display JEDEC and SFDP information once (while idle)
  ERASE FFF000 - confirm ONE destructive flash test (see warning below)
IMU printing: OFF (default after boot)
WARNING: destructive flash test is DISARMED.
Confirmation permanently erases ALL 4096 bytes at 0xFFF000-0xFFFFFF.
It then writes 256 test bytes at 0xFFF000-0xFFF0FF; data is not restored.
To authorise exactly ONE test, send this exact line followed by Enter:
ERASE FFF000
IMU ON / IMU OFF control printing. Reboot never schedules a destructive test.
